cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, methodology, or published search records, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "SETIsearch: Panchromatic (8.273-Octave, 0.0905-28.00 um) Space-Lyman to JWST Thermal-IR, Optical, Near-IR Echelle Laser, Frequency-Comb, Radio & Photometric Technosignature Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Prospectively locked, reproducible archival searches and pure-stdlib numerical audits
  for panchromatic space Lyman-limit/FUV/NUV (FUSE 0.0905-0.1187 um, HST/COS G130M
  0.1125-0.1450 um, HST/STIS E140M 0.1145-0.1710 um, HST/STIS E230M/E230H 0.1605-0.3150 um),
  ground near-UV (VLT UVES_NUV), optical (HARPS, HARPS-N, ESPRESSO HR/UHR, OHP SOPHIE,
  OHP ELODIE, CFHT ESPaDOnS), far-red (VLT UVES_RED, CARMENES_VIS), near-infrared YJH
  (NIRPS_HE), thermal K-band (VLT CRIRES+), simultaneous YJHK (CFHT SPIRou APERO
  0.7.295), and JWST space thermal-IR (NIRSpec G235H 1.655-3.072 um, NIRSpec G395H
  2.862-5.179 um, MIRI MRS Ch1-4 4.900-28.00 um including Townes 10.60 um CO2 laser and
  Project Hephaistos OBJECT_D/OBJECT_E) laser and periodic frequency-comb technosignatures
  (0.0905-28.00 um, 8.273 unbroken octaves across 16 spectrographs / 19 arms plus FEROS;
  280 unique stars and 1,920 archival exposures totaling 587.0558 h across V3.0-V4.1 +
  COMB_V4_1 with Keplerian planetary de-Doppler, G4_V41 MIRI dual-subband / FUSE
  dual-channel / Fiber-B vetoes, 2D CCD/MAMA/COS/H2RG/H4RG/JWST vetoes, sparse G6
  coincidence gating, and uniform all-sky COMB_V4_1 matched filtering across 100% of
  D079-D090 / 321 stacks), unified with planetary-rest-frame 1.4 GHz narrowband radio
  searches (Parkes/GBT) and TESS specular light-sail photometry achieving 23/23 (100%)
  radio-echelle closure across a 280-system multi-messenger synthesis (0 verified ETI
  detections; 0.0973 W HST_STIS Proxima Cen, 0.2194 W HST_COS GJ 832, 0.4294 W FUSE
  Alpha Cen A, 228.98 W JWST_MIRI_MRS WISE0855 at 5.80 um, and 2.7047 kW VMA2 at 10.60 um).
